def add(label,needle,claims,refs,remaining='Complete animation helper timing/host pixels, all catalogue vectors and every downstream combination remain separate; no whole-domain closure.'):
 loc=[n+1 for n,line in enumerate(ft.splitlines()) if needle in line];assert loc,(label,needle);n=len(rows)+1;rows.append(dict(id=f'CEC-R{n:03}',label=label,formal=dict(path=formal,matching_lines=loc),premise='Fixed reference commit, valid ordinary Pokemon/player/Pokedex/Bag and declared caller values. Reached prior host, message, media, animation and data steps return normally unless the failure prefix is stated. No external hook/plugin assumed; no business execution.',child_assertions=[dict(id=f'CEC-R{n:03}-A{i:02}',meaning=c,source_units=refs,status='BOUNDED_ACTUAL_SOURCE_AND_RECEIVER_SUPPORTED',whole_parent_acceptance=False) for i,c in enumerate(claims,1)],normal_cancel_failure='No transaction/rescue/rollback surrounds this chain. Only writes reached before cancellation or exception persist; later model/Dex/move learning/outer item removal and cleanup are not guaranteed after an earlier failure.',remaining=remaining,accepted=False))
add('FIVE_FAMILIES_GUARDS','### 4.1',[ 'All five wrappers delegate the same individual to check_evolution_internal, adding only their own family callback and actual item/other Pokemon/party index/event value; event value defaults 0.','Common short circuit order is egg? OR shadowPokemon?, then hasItem(EVERSTONE), then hasAbility(BATTLEBOND); any match returns nil before callback scanning.','Current species_data.get_evolutions(true) supplies ordered current species/form forward triples; Species removes prevolution and None before the redundant evo[3] guard.','The first truthy callback outcome maps to its corresponding target symbol; later entries are not tested. An absent family proc returns false via its registry call wrapper rather than promoting after-action-only Shedinja.','The callbacks do not commit species/EXP/moves. Guard/predicate getters can fill derived caches, while EventAfterDamageTaken is the explicit domain write to ready_to_evolve; no all-bytes-unchanged claim.'],['pokemon:check_evolution_on_level_up','pokemon:check_evolution_on_use_item','pokemon:check_evolution_on_trade','pokemon:check_evolution_after_battle','pokemon:check_evolution_by_event','pokemon:check_evolution_internal','species:get_evolutions'])
add('MINIMUM_LEVEL_FAMILY','最小等级数据推导',[ 'Minimum level is 1 with no relations/no selected reverse relation; it consumes the first reverse prevolution selected by the compiler, rather than reselecting all candidate parents.','It resolves prevo species with this base_form and returns 1 if that prevo has nonnil incense, before recursing to its minimum.','When method lacks level_up_proc and is not Shedinja it returns prevo minimum; otherwise any_level_up truthy gives prevo minimum+1, else the literal parameter.','This query is not a guard inside the five check wrappers. Legal acyclic inputs are the scope; recursive family/baby/minimum queries do not establish arbitrary-cycle termination.','Family enumeration sorts targets by registry key order; get_evolutions preserves authored order. Family include-None queries and runtime exclude-None queries are different consumers.','Baby-species walks the selected first reverse relation and optional incense items; egg-move fallback uses that prevo and current form, not a merge of every possible ancestral branch.'],['species:minimum_level','species:get_evolutions','species:get_family_evolutions','species:get_baby_species','species:get_family_species','species:get_egg_moves'])
add('PREPARE_CANCEL_COMMIT','### 5.1',[ 'StartScreen builds both old/target sprites before animation; target starts invisible. set_up_animation schedules both visible at time0, target zoom0 and white alpha255, before any success mutation.','pbEvolution performs initial text/decision/old cry and one-second update wait before Evolution start ME and Evolution BGM; only its later animation loop tests BACK && cancancel.','On accepted BACK it stops BGM, plays cancel SE and breaks with canceled=true; flash/reset runs before cancellation statistic/message.','Cancellation increments evolutions_cancelled and displays stopped text; it never calls pbEvolutionSuccess, hence no success count/after-action/model/Dex/new evolution move writes from this sequence.','If flash/update/message raises, even the later cancellation count or message may be absent. Prior caller level/EXP/happiness/learned moves are not reverted.','Natural animation completion calls success after its flash; no recheck of original predicate, environment, item eligibility or guard is made between candidate selection and commit.'],['ui:pbStartScreen','ui:set_up_animation','ui:pbEvolution','ui:pbFlashInOut'])
add('SUCCESS_PREFIX','### 5.2',[ 'Success first increments evolution_count, obtains new-species cry length with the individual current form, plays cry, waits, stops BGM, plays success ME and shows congratulations using old display name and new species name.','After-action scan runs before original species mutation. A failure in presentation can leave success count incremented while neither after-actions nor model commit occurred.','After actions, success records old fainted state, sets species, writes hp=0 if old fainted, explicitly calc_stats again and clears ready_to_evolve.','It then snapshots was_owned, registers the actual mutated individual and sets new species owned, before collecting new level0/current-level moves in their ordered learning list.','Optional MoreOften && !was_owned && has_pokedex && species_in_unlocked_dex gate shows the added-data message, registers last_seen and opens Dex entry; those failure points do not undo prior model/Dex writes.','With no pending moves that Dex path calls pbEndScreen(false) early; otherwise moves each pass general pbLearnMove(...,true), whose refusal affects that move only. Caller still contains its own final EndScreen; host repeat disposal is not guaranteed.'],['ui:pbEvolutionSuccess','ui:pbEvolutionMethodAfterEvolution','pokemon:action_after_evolution','utilities:pbLearnMove','ui:pbEndScreen'])
add('SPECIES_MUTATION_RETENTION','### 5.4',[ 'species= resolves target and returns immediately when target.base species equals current stored species. An actual base-species change sets species, selects nonnegative target default_form else positive target form else preserves stored form.','On a real change it clears forced_form, gender only when singleGendered?, level cache and ability value, then calc_stats; ability_index is retained.','The setter does not overwrite Owner/PID/IV/EV/nature/nickname/ribbons/markings/obtain/breeding fields. Their dependent reads and later evolution move learning remain separately scoped.','The explicit post-set faint-preservation and second calc_stats are reached only after normal species= return. Clear-ready follows both, so an earlier error can leave a partial model prefix.'],['pokemon:species=','ui:pbEvolutionSuccess'])
add('AFTER_ACTION_ORDER_AND_DUPLICATE','### 5.3',[ 'After-action scan uses the old species_data ordered forward non-None triples and stops on first truthy call_after_evolution. Held-item callbacks independently require actual new target equal their row target and still-held required item.','Shedinja callback does not compare actual evo target with its own row target: it checks party_full? first, then Bag has POKEBALL, duplicates to the Shedinja row target, removes one POKEBALL and returns true. Ordinary Nincada data chooses Ninjask through its level callback.','Duplicate clones before original species mutation, sets duplicate species, clears name/markings/item/ribbons, resets ball POKEBALL, calc_stats and full heal, then appends the same duplicate object to player party.','It registers that duplicate and marks target owned before the callback removes the ball. An error after append can leave party/Dex prefix and prevent ball removal or original evolution.','Full/ball-absent returns false without duplication and allows further after-action scan; those ordinary refusals do not cancel original evolution success.','clone copies IV/IVmaxed/EV hashes, each Move, first_moves, Owner and ribbons, while shallow inherited scalar identity/PID remains; duplicate markings are independently reset. This is not a new randomly generated individual or a new PID.'],['pokemon:action_after_evolution','pokemon:clone','evolution:Shedinja','ui:self.pbDuplicatePokemon','ui:pbEvolutionSuccess'])
add('CANDY_CONSUMPTION_BOUNDARY','稀有糖果·满级分支',[ 'RARECANDY handler explicitly rejects Shadow first. Below maximum it plays level-up SE, calls ChangeLevel(current+qty), hard-refreshes and returns true regardless evolution cancellation.','At maximum it computes level-family target, then requires RARE_CANDY_USABLE_AT_MAX_LEVEL and target. Failure shows no-effect and false; successful candidate uses cancellable default Evolution, EndScreen, optional refresh, then true even when canceled.','The maximum branch changes no level itself; any_level_up callbacks can pass because they contain no event-history guard. Maximum quantity helper max_level-level returning0 does not itself become an unconditional no-use guard in the two ordinary callers.','UseItem and UseItemOnPokemon choose qty1 initially and show quantity chooser only max_at_once>1; after true return they remove qty only when the item consumed_after_use? flag applies.','UseItemOnPokemon clears annotations/hard-refreshes before removal; an exception there can preserve consumed handler/model prefix without removing Bag quantity. UseItem removes before its last-item message.','Declining choice/qty<=0 or handler false avoids that outer removal; cancellation of evolution is not handler false and does not roll back prior candy level or learning.'],['effects:RareCandyMaximum','effects:RareCandy','utilities:pbChangeLevel','utilities:pbUseItem','utilities:pbUseItemOnPokemon'])
add('STONE_AND_EVENT_ENTRY','进化石（道具）',[ 'Evolution-stone dynamic handler requires Item is_evolution_stone, rejects Shadow with a message, checks actual item-family target and runs Evolution(false), EndScreen and optional party annotations/refresh before returning true.','Normal handler success delegates Bag decrement to the two item-use callers and consumed_after_use flag; there is no input cancel within Evolution(false). Missing target returns false/no-effect.','Bag opening annotations are computed before showing the party screen; actual use invokes the predicate again, and after normal evolution party annotations are recomputed against current species.','General Bag caller invokes pbCheckUseOnPokemon before handler. Bare handler invocation is not granted the full caller eligibility contract and no universal nil/invalid-object protection is invented.','Individual trigger_event_evolution returns false without target, otherwise runs cancellable Evolution and EndScreen then true even if canceled; it does not introduce global one-use event-ID state.'],['effects:EvolutionStones','utilities:pbUseItem','utilities:pbUseItemOnPokemon','utilities:pbCheckUseOnPokemon','pokemon:trigger_event_evolution'])
add('LEVEL_EXP_ENTRY_PREFIX','等级设置辅助·升级分支',[ 'ChangeLevel records requested capped level and writes level/stats before its change-specific presentation, happiness and crossed level learning; upward branch checks evolution only after that learning.','ChangeExp similarly writes new exp/recalculates stats first; gained-exp branch then handles happiness, level message/moves and level-family target. Lower or equal paths do not acquire an invented any-level-up evolution trigger.','Both wrappers invoke default cancellable Evolution and caller EndScreen. Canceling preserves previous EXP/level/HP/stat/happiness/move writes; later UI exception prevents later steps without restoring them.','These callers do not consume held evolution items or Shedinja ball before success after-actions. Any triggering Bag item belongs to outer item handler consumption.'],['utilities:pbChangeLevel','utilities:pbChangeExp','ui:pbEvolution','ui:pbEvolutionSuccess'])
out=dict(schema='gr8-cre-c-wp31-wrappers-commit/v1',recorded_utc=utc,actual_reader=reader,formal_identity=dict(path=formal,bytes=len(fraw),sha256=hashlib.sha256(fraw).hexdigest(),git_blob=subprocess.check_output(['git','-C',str(B),'rev-parse','fd1df570cad987dc3852a3b958f03916e317f7fe:'+formal],text=True).strip()),source_identities=ids,whole_source_units=units,records=rows,manual_atoms=sum(len(x['child_assertions']) for x in rows),mandatory_previous_packets=['wp31-registry-meaning-atoms.v1.json','wp32-context-meaning.v1.json','pbs-evolution-reception.v1.json'],unknown_method_metadata_review='wp31-unknown-method-note-review-request.v1.json; pending root adjudication, no formal finding.',scope_remaining='Precise animation timing helper semantics and remaining formal/shared catalogue compounds still require subsequent review. This bounded unit is not full WP31/A/C acceptance.',denominator_frozen=False,new_votes=0,business='NOT_EXECUTED',update='UPDATE_NOT_STARTED')
f=P/'wp31-wrappers-commit-meaning.v1.json';assert not f.exists();f.write_text(json.dumps(out,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n');rev=json.loads((P/'reverse-mapping.json').read_text());assert not any(x['id'].startswith('CEC-') for x in rev['records']);rev['records']+=rows;rev['utc']=utc;(P/'reverse-mapping.json').write_text(json.dumps(rev,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n');pr=json.loads((P/'progress.json').read_text());pr['updated_utc']=utc;pr['primary_clause_atoms']=sum(len(x.get('child_assertions',[])) for x in rev['records']);(P/'progress.json').write_text(json.dumps(pr,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n');raw=f.read_bytes();print(json.dumps(dict(utc=utc,bytes=len(raw),sha256=hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),groups=len(rows),atoms=out['manual_atoms'],units=len(units),current_all_manual_atoms=pr['primary_clause_atoms'])))
